{
  "Makefile": "- File Path: `Makefile`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines a set of convenient commands (targets) for building, running, stopping, and managing the GoTrade microservices application using Docker Compose.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Variables:\n        - `DOCKER_COMPOSE`: String, module-level, set to `docker-compose`.\n    - Functions / Methods (Targets):\n        - `all`: Public target, default command, calls `up`.\n        - `build`: Public target, builds Docker images for all services.\n        - `up`: Public target, starts all services in detached mode, rebuilding images.\n        - `down`: Public target, stops and removes all services, networks, and volumes.\n        - `restart`: Public target, restarts all services by first calling `down` then `up`.\n        - `logs`: Public target, tails logs from all running services.\n        - `restart-service`: Public target, restarts a specific service identified by the `service` variable.\n        - `test`: Public target, placeholder for running application tests.\n        - `lint`: Public target, placeholder for running code linters.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Uses `.PHONY` to declare targets that are not actual files. Leverages shell commands to interact with `docker-compose`.\n",
  "README.md": "- File Path: `README.md`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a comprehensive overview of the GoTrade project, detailing its architecture, prerequisites, setup instructions, development commands, and descriptions of individual microservices and API endpoints.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Sections:\n        - `GoTrade - A Golang Microservices Trading Platform`: High-level description of the project as an event-driven trading platform.\n        - `Architecture`: Describes the system's microservices, communication via REST and Redis Pub/Sub, and the role of Nginx as an API Gateway. Includes an ASCII diagram illustrating the service interactions.\n        - `Prerequisites`: Lists necessary software (Docker, Go, make).\n        - `Setup \u0026 Running`: Provides steps to clone the repository, configure environment variables (`.env`), and start/stop the application using `make up`/`make down`.\n        - `Development Commands`: Lists `make` targets for common development tasks like `build`, `up`, `down`, `restart`, `logs`, `restart-service`, `test`, `lint`.\n        - `Service Descriptions`: Briefly explains the role of each microservice (Nginx, user-service, instrument-service, order-service, account-service, websocket-gateway, PostgreSQL, Redis).\n        - `API Documentation`: Lists primary API endpoints for each service.\n        - `Environment Variables`: Mentions configuration via environment variables and refers to `.env.example`.\n",
  "account-service/Dockerfile": "- File Path: `account-service/Dockerfile`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines a multi-stage Docker build process to create a minimal and efficient Docker image for the Go `account-service` application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Stages:\n        - `builder`: Uses `golang:1.21-alpine` to download Go modules and build the `server` binary with `CGO_ENABLED=0` for a static executable.\n        - Final image: Uses `alpine:latest` as a base, adds `ca-certificates`, copies the pre-built binary from the `builder` stage, exposes port 8084, and defines the command to run the service.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Multi-stage build for smaller image size, static compilation of Go application, minimal base image for production.\n",
  "account-service/cmd/server/main.go": "- File Path: `account-service/cmd/server/main.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: The main entry point for the `account-service` application, responsible for configuration loading, database initialization, dependency injection, HTTP routing, and server lifecycle management.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions:\n        - `main()`: Public function.\n            - Loads environment variables from `.env`.\n            - Retrieves `APP_PORT`, `POSTGRES_URL`, and `JWT_SECRET` from environment variables, exiting if critical ones are missing.\n            - Initializes a PostgreSQL connection pool and runs database migrations (`accounts` and `transactions` table creation).\n            - Sets up the application layers: `repository.NewPostgresAccountRepository`, `usecase.NewAccountUsecase`, `handler.NewAccountHandler`.\n            - Configures an HTTP router using `go-chi/chi`, including `middleware.Logger` and `middleware.Recoverer`.\n            - Defines public routes (`/health`, `/metrics`).\n            - Defines protected routes (`/account`, `/account/transfer`) using `handler.JWTAuthMiddleware`.\n            - Starts the HTTP server and implements graceful shutdown on `SIGINT` or `SIGTERM`.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Dependency Injection, Layered Architecture (handler -\u003e usecase -\u003e repository -\u003e database), Graceful Shutdown, Environment Variable Configuration, HTTP Routing with Chi.\n",
  "account-service/go.mod": "- File Path: `account-service/go.mod`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the Go module for the `account-service` and lists its direct and indirect dependencies.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Module: `gotrade/account-service`\n    - Go Version: `1.21`\n    - Required Dependencies:\n        - `github.com/go-chi/chi/v5 v5.0.12`: For HTTP routing.\n        - `github.com/golang-jwt/jwt/v5 v5.2.1`: For JWT token handling.\n        - `github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 v5.5.5`: PostgreSQL driver.\n        - `github.com/joho/godotenv v1.5.1`: For loading environment variables from `.env` files.\n    - Indirect Dependencies: Includes `github.com/jackc/pgpassfile`, `github.com/jackc/pgservicefile`, `github.com/jackc/puddle/v2`, `golang.org/x/crypto`, `golang.org/x/sync`, `golang.org/x/text`.\n",
  "account-service/internal/domain/account.go": "- File Path: `account-service/internal/domain/account.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the core `Account` and `Transaction` entities, along with related types and constants, used within the `account-service` domain.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Types:\n        - `TransactionType`: String type for transaction types.\n    - Constants:\n        - `Deposit`: `TransactionType` constant.\n        - `Withdrawal`: `TransactionType` constant.\n    - Structs:\n        - `Account`: Represents a user's financial account.\n            - `ID`: `int64`, unique identifier.\n            - `UserID`: `int64`, ID of the user who owns the account.\n            - `Balance`: `float64`, current balance.\n            - `Currency`: `string`, currency type (default 'USD').\n            - `CreatedAt`: `time.Time`, timestamp of creation.\n            - `UpdatedAt`: `time.Time`, timestamp of last update.\n        - `Transaction`: Represents a financial transaction on an account.\n            - `ID`: `int64`, unique identifier.\n            - `AccountID`: `int64`, ID of the associated account.\n            - `Type`: `TransactionType`, type of transaction (Deposit/Withdrawal).\n            - `Amount`: `float64`, amount of the transaction.\n            - `Timestamp`: `time.Time`, timestamp of the transaction.\n",
  "account-service/internal/handler/account_handler.go": "- File Path: `account-service/internal/handler/account_handler.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements HTTP handlers for account-related API endpoints, translating HTTP requests into usecase calls and formatting responses.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Structs:\n        - `AccountHandler`: Holds a reference to the `usecase.AccountUsecase` to perform business logic.\n        - `FundTransferRequest`: Represents the expected JSON payload for fund transfer requests, with `Type` (DEPOSIT/WITHDRAWAL) and `Amount` fields.\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewAccountHandler(uc usecase.AccountUsecase) *AccountHandler`: Public function. Constructor for `AccountHandler`.\n    - Methods:\n        - `GetAccount(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public method on `AccountHandler`. Handles requests to retrieve the authenticated user's account details. Extracts `userID` from the request context, calls `accountUsecase.GetAccountByUserID`, and responds with the account data or an error.\n        - `FundTransfer(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public method on `AccountHandler`. Handles requests for depositing or withdrawing funds. Extracts `userID` from context, decodes the request body, validates the amount and type, calls `accountUsecase.Deposit` or `accountUsecase.Withdraw`, and responds with the updated account info or appropriate error status (e.g., `400 Bad Request` for invalid input or `ErrInsufficientFunds`).\n",
  "account-service/internal/handler/auth_middleware.go": "- File Path: `account-service/internal/handler/auth_middleware.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements an HTTP middleware for authenticating requests using JWT tokens for the `account-service`.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions:\n        - `JWTAuthMiddleware(secret string) func(http.Handler) http.Handler`: Public function. A higher-order function that returns an `http.Handler` middleware. This middleware extracts a JWT from the \"Authorization\" header (Bearer token), validates it using `utils.ValidateJWT`, and if valid, extracts the `UserID` from the token claims and adds it to the request context before passing the request to the next handler. It returns `401 Unauthorized` for missing, malformed, or invalid tokens.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Standard Go HTTP middleware pattern, specifically a JWT authentication middleware.\n",
  "account-service/internal/platform/database/postgres.go": "- File Path: `account-service/internal/platform/database/postgres.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Manages the PostgreSQL database connection pool and initial schema setup for the `account-service`, including `accounts` and `transactions` tables.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewPostgresPool(connStr string) (*pgxpool.Pool, error)`: Public function. Creates and configures a new PostgreSQL connection pool using `pgxpool`. It parses the connection string, sets default pool settings (max connections, lifetime, idle time, health check), and pings the database to verify connectivity.\n        - `InitDatabase(pool *pgxpool.Pool) error`: Public function. Executes SQL to create the `accounts` table (with `user_id` unique constraint) and the `transactions` table (with foreign key to `accounts`) if they do not already exist. This function is intended for initial database setup or migrations.\n",
  "account-service/internal/repository/account_repository.go": "- File Path: `account-service/internal/repository/account_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the interface for data access operations related to `Account` and `Transaction` entities, abstracting the underlying data storage mechanism.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Interfaces:\n        - `AccountRepository`: Defines the contract for account and transaction data persistence.\n            - `GetByUserID(ctx context.Context, userID int64) (*domain.Account, error)`: Public method. Retrieves an account by its user ID.\n            - `Create(ctx context.Context, account *domain.Account) error`: Public method. Inserts a new account into the data store.\n            - `UpdateBalanceInTx(ctx context.Context, tx pgx.Tx, accountID int64, newBalance float64) error`: Public method. Updates an account's balance within a transaction.\n            - `CreateTransactionInTx(ctx context.Context, tx pgx.Tx, transaction *domain.Transaction) error`: Public method. Creates a new transaction record within a transaction.\n            - `RunWithTransaction(ctx context.Context, fn func(tx pgx.Tx) error) error`: Public method. Executes a function within a database transaction.\n",
  "account-service/internal/repository/account_repository_postgres.go": "- File Path: `account-service/internal/repository/account_repository_postgres.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a PostgreSQL-specific implementation of the `AccountRepository` interface, handling database interactions for account and transaction data, including transactional operations.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Structs:\n        - `postgresAccountRepository`: Implements `AccountRepository`, holding a `pgxpool.Pool` instance for database access.\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewPostgresAccountRepository(db *pgxpool.Pool) AccountRepository`: Public function. Constructor for `postgresAccountRepository`.\n    - Methods:\n        - `GetByUserID(ctx context.Context, userID int64) (*domain.Account, error)`: Public method on `postgresAccountRepository`. Retrieves an account by its `userID`. Returns `nil, nil` if no account is found.\n        - `Create(ctx context.Context, account *domain.Account) error`: Public method on `postgresAccountRepository`. Inserts a new account record into the `accounts` table, returning the generated `id`, `created_at`, and `updated_at` values.\n        - `UpdateBalanceInTx(ctx context.Context, tx pgx.Tx, accountID int64, newBalance float64) error`: Public method on `postgresAccountRepository`. Updates the `balance` and `updated_at` fields of an account within a provided PostgreSQL transaction.\n        - `CreateTransactionInTx(ctx context.Context, tx pgx.Tx, transaction *domain.Transaction) error`: Public method on `postgresAccountRepository`. Inserts a new transaction record into the `transactions` table within a provided PostgreSQL transaction.\n        - `RunWithTransaction(ctx context.Context, fn func(tx pgx.Tx) error) error`: Public method on `postgresAccountRepository`. Executes a given function `fn` within a new PostgreSQL transaction, handling commit and rollback.\n",
  "account-service/internal/usecase/account_usecase.go": "- File Path: `account-service/internal/usecase/account_usecase.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements the business logic for account management, including retrieving, depositing, and withdrawing funds, ensuring transactional integrity.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Interfaces:\n        - `AccountUsecase`: Defines the contract for account-related business operations.\n            - `GetAccountByUserID(ctx context.Context, userID int64) (*AccountInfo, error)`: Public method. Retrieves account information for a user.\n            - `Deposit(ctx context.Context, userID int64, amount float64) (*AccountInfo, error)`: Public method. Handles depositing funds into a user's account.\n            - `Withdraw(ctx context.Context, userID int64, amount float64) (*AccountInfo, error)`: Public method. Handles withdrawing funds from a user's account.\n    - Structs:\n        - `AccountInfo`: Represents a simplified view of account data for API responses.\n            - `UserID`: `int64`.\n            - `Balance`: `float64`.\n            - `Currency`: `string`.\n        - `accountUsecase`: Implements `AccountUsecase`, holding a reference to `repository.AccountRepository`.\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewAccountUsecase(repo repository.AccountRepository) AccountUsecase`: Public function. Constructor for `accountUsecase`.\n    - Methods:\n        - `getOrCreateAccount(ctx context.Context, userID int64) (*domain.Account, error)`: Internal method on `accountUsecase`. Retrieves an account by `userID`, creating a new one with initial mock funds (100,000 USD) if it doesn't exist.\n        - `GetAccountByUserID(ctx context.Context, userID int64) (*AccountInfo, error)`: Public method on `accountUsecase`. Retrieves or creates an account for the given user and returns its `AccountInfo`.\n        - `Deposit(ctx context.Context, userID int64, amount float64) (*AccountInfo, error)`: Public method on `accountUsecase`. Performs a deposit operation. It uses `RunWithTransaction` to atomically update the account balance and create a transaction record. Returns `ErrAccountNotFound` if the account doesn't exist.\n        - `Withdraw(ctx context.Context, userID int64, amount float64) (*AccountInfo, error)`: Public method on `accountUsecase`. Performs a withdrawal operation. It uses `RunWithTransaction` to atomically update the account balance and create a transaction record. Returns `ErrInsufficientFunds` if the balance is too low, or `ErrAccountNotFound`.\n    - Variables:\n        - `ErrInsufficientFunds`: `error`, module-level, exported.\n        - `ErrAccountNotFound`: `error`, module-level, exported.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Encapsulates business rules, uses exported errors for specific error conditions, orchestrates calls to repository functions, ensures transactional integrity for fund transfers.\n",
  "account-service/pkg/utils/jwt.go": "- File Path: `account-service/pkg/utils/jwt.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides utility functions for generating and validating JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) within the `account-service`.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Structs:\n        - `JWTClaims`: Custom JWT claims structure, embedding `jwt.RegisteredClaims` and adding a `UserID` field.\n            - `UserID`: `int64`, the ID of the user.\n            - `RegisteredClaims`: Standard JWT claims (e.g., `ExpiresAt`, `IssuedAt`).\n    - Functions:\n        - `GenerateJWT(userID int64, secret string) (string, error)`: Public function. Creates a new JWT token for a given `userID`, signing it with the provided `secret`. The token includes `user_id`, `expiration` (72 hours), and `issued at` claims.\n        - `ValidateJWT(tokenString string, secret string) (*jwt.Token, error)`: Public function. Parses and validates a JWT `tokenString` using the provided `secret` and `JWTClaims` structure. It ensures the signing method is HMAC.\n",
  "docker-compose.yml": "- File Path: `docker-compose.yml`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines and configures the multi-service Docker application for GoTrade, orchestrating the deployment and networking of all microservices, databases, and gateways.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Version: `3.8`\n    - Services:\n        - `nginx`: Nginx API Gateway, routes traffic, depends on all services.\n        - `user-service`: Go user microservice, builds from `./user-service`, exposes 8081, depends on `postgres`.\n        - `instrument-service`: Go instrument microservice, builds from `./instrument-service`, exposes 8082, depends on `postgres`.\n        - `instrument-seeder`: One-off service to seed instrument data, builds from `./instrument-service/scripts/seed/Dockerfile`, depends on a healthy `postgres`, restarts on failure.\n        - `order-service`: Go order microservice, builds from `./order-service`, exposes 8083, depends on `postgres` and `redis`.\n        - `account-service`: Go account microservice, builds from `./account-service`, exposes 8084, depends on `postgres`.\n        - `websocket-gateway`: Go WebSocket gateway, builds from `./websocket-gateway`, exposes 8085, depends on `redis`.\n        - `postgres`: PostgreSQL database, uses `postgres:14-alpine` image, exposes 5432, defines environment variables for user/password/db, uses a named volume for data, includes a healthcheck.\n        - `redis`: Redis in-memory data store, uses `redis:7-alpine` image, exposes 6379.\n    - Networks:\n        - `gotrade-net`: A bridge network connecting all services.\n    - Volumes:\n        - `postgres-data`: A named volume for PostgreSQL persistent data.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Microservices architecture, Docker Compose for orchestration, service discovery via network aliases, environment variable injection, health checks for database, named volumes for data persistence, multi-service dependencies.\n",
  "frontend/index.html": "- File Path: `frontend/index.html`\n- High-Level Purpose: Serves as the single-page application (SPA) frontend for the GoTrade platform, providing user authentication (login), a trading dashboard, watchlist, order entry, open orders, order history, and a real-time event log.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - HTML Structure:\n        - `head`: Includes Tailwind CSS for styling and custom scrollbar styles.\n        - `body`:\n            - `login-view`: Contains a login form with email and password fields, and an error display.\n            - `app-view`: (Initially hidden) Contains the main trading interface.\n                - `header`: Displays the app title, user email, and a logout button.\n                - `main`:\n                    - `dashboard-section`: Shows account balance.\n                    - `watchlist` section: Allows adding instruments to a watchlist via a dropdown and displays them in a table.\n                    - `order-entry` section: A form for placing new orders (instrument, side, type, quantity, price).\n                    - `open-orders` section: Displays current open orders in a table with a cancel option.\n                    - `order-history` section: Displays past orders in a table.\n                    - `real-time-log` section: A scrollable container for real-time event messages.\n    - CSS Styling:\n        - Uses Tailwind CSS for utility-first styling.\n        - Custom CSS for scrollbar appearance.\n    - JavaScript (within `\u003cscript\u003e` tag):\n        - Constants:\n            - `API_BASE_URL`: `/api`, base path for API calls.\n            - `WS_URL`: `ws://${window.location.host}/ws`, WebSocket endpoint.\n        - Variables:\n            - `state`: Object, module-level. Manages application state including `token` (from localStorage), `user`, `account`, `instruments`, `watchlist` (from localStorage), `openOrders`, `orderHistory`, and `ws` (WebSocket instance).\n            - Numerous DOM element references (e.g., `loginView`, `appView`, `loginForm`, `userEmailEl`, `logoutBtn`, `accountDetailsEl`, `watchlistForm`, `orderForm`, `logContainer`, etc.).\n        - Functions:\n            - `apiFetch(endpoint, options)`: Public, async. Handles HTTP requests to the backend, including JWT authorization, JSON parsing, and error handling. Automatically logs out on 401 Unauthorized responses.\n            - `connectWebSocket()`: Public. Establishes a WebSocket connection, sets up `onopen`, `onmessage`, `onclose`, and `onerror` handlers. Reconnects automatically on close. Processes incoming messages, triggering order refreshes for \"Order\" related events.\n            - `renderAccount()`: Public. Updates the displayed account balance.\n            - `renderInstrumentSelectors()`: Public. Populates the instrument dropdowns for watchlist and order entry.\n            - `renderWatchlist()`: Public. Renders the watchlist table based on `state.watchlist` and `state.instruments`.\n            - `renderOrders()`: Public. Renders the open orders and order history tables.\n            - `addLogMessage(message)`: Public. Appends a timestamped message to the real-time event log.\n            - `fetchAccount()`: Public, async. Fetches the authenticated user's account details.\n            - `fetchInstruments()`: Public, async. Fetches all available trading instruments.\n            - `fetchOrders()`: Public, async. Fetches both open orders and order history.\n            - `handleLogin(event)`: Public, async. Processes login form submission, calls `/user/login`, stores the JWT token, and initializes the app view.\n            - `logout()`: Public. Clears the JWT token, user data, closes WebSocket, and switches back to the login view.\n            - `handleAddWatchlist(event)`: Public. Adds a selected instrument to the `watchlist` in state and localStorage, then re-renders the watchlist.\n            - `handleRemoveWatchlist(event)`: Public. Removes an instrument from the `watchlist` in state and localStorage, then re-renders.\n            - `handlePlaceOrder(event)`: Public, async. Processes order placement form submission, calls `/orders/`, and triggers an order refresh.\n            - `handleCancelOrder(event)`: Public, async. Handles clicking the \"Cancel\" button for an open order, calls `/orders/{orderId}` with DELETE method, and triggers an order refresh.\n            - `showView(viewName)`: Public. Toggles visibility between the login and app views.\n            - `loadAppData()`: Public, async. Orchestrates fetching initial account, instrument, and order data, and connects the WebSocket.\n            - `init()`: Public, async. The main application initialization function. Checks for an existing JWT token, attempts to fetch user profile, and either displays the app view or the login view.\n        - Event Listeners:\n            - `DOMContentLoaded`: Calls `init()` when the page loads.\n            - `loginForm` `submit`: `handleLogin`.\n            - `logoutBtn` `click`: `logout`.\n            - `watchlistForm` `submit`: `handleAddWatchlist`.\n            - `watchlistTableBody` `click`: `handleRemoveWatchlist` (delegated).\n            - `orderForm` `submit`: `handlePlaceOrder`.\n            - `openOrdersTableBody` `click`: `handleCancelOrder` (delegated).\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Single-Page Application (SPA), client-side JWT authentication, REST API interaction, WebSocket for real-time updates, local storage for client-side persistence (JWT, watchlist), dynamic DOM manipulation for UI rendering, event delegation for table actions.",
  "instrument-service/Dockerfile": "- File Path: `instrument-service/Dockerfile`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines a multi-stage Docker build process to create a minimal and efficient Docker image for the Go `instrument-service` application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Stages:\n        - `builder`: Uses `golang:1.21-alpine` to download Go modules and build the `instrument-service` binary with `CGO_ENABLED=0` for a static executable.\n        - Final image: Uses `alpine:latest` as a base, adds `ca-certificates`, copies the pre-built binary from the `builder` stage, exposes port 8082, and defines the command to run the service.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Multi-stage build for smaller image size, static compilation of Go application, minimal base image for production.\n",
  "instrument-service/cmd/server/main.go": "- File Path: `instrument-service/cmd/server/main.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: The main entry point for the `instrument-service` application, responsible for configuration loading, database initialization, dependency injection, HTTP routing, and server lifecycle management.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions:\n        - `main()`: Public function.\n            - Loads environment variables from `.env`.\n            - Retrieves `APP_PORT` and `POSTGRES_URL` from environment variables.\n            - Initializes a PostgreSQL connection pool and runs database migrations (`instruments` table creation).\n            - Sets up the application layers: `repository.NewPostgresInstrumentRepository`, `usecase.NewInstrumentUsecase`, `handler.NewInstrumentHandler`.\n            - Configures an HTTP router using `go-chi/chi`, including `middleware.Logger` and `middleware.Recoverer`.\n            - Defines public routes (`/health`, `/metrics`, `/instruments`).\n            - Starts the HTTP server and implements graceful shutdown on `SIGINT` or `SIGTERM`.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Dependency Injection, Layered Architecture (handler -\u003e usecase -\u003e repository -\u003e database), Graceful Shutdown, Environment Variable Configuration, HTTP Routing with Chi.\n",
  "instrument-service/go.mod": "- File Path: `instrument-service/go.mod`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the Go module for the `instrument-service` and lists its direct dependencies.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Module: `gotrade/instrument-service`\n    - Go Version: `1.21`\n    - Required Dependencies:\n        - `github.com/go-chi/chi/v5 v5.0.12`: For HTTP routing.\n        - `github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 v5.5.5`: PostgreSQL driver.\n        - `github.com/joho/godotenv v1.5.1`: For loading environment variables from `.env` files.\n",
  "instrument-service/internal/domain/instrument.go": "- File Path: `instrument-service/internal/domain/instrument.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the core `Instrument` entity structure used throughout the `instrument-service` domain.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Types:\n        - `InstrumentType`: String type for instrument types (e.g., EQUITY, FUTURE, OPTION).\n    - Constants:\n        - `Equity`, `Future`, `Option`: `InstrumentType` constants.\n    - Structs:\n        - `Instrument`: Represents a tradable financial instrument.\n            - `ID`: `int64`, unique identifier.\n            - `Symbol`: `string`, trading symbol (e.g., \"RELIANCE\").\n            - `Name`: `string`, full name of the instrument.\n            - `Type`: `InstrumentType`, type of the instrument.\n            - `Exchange`: `string`, exchange where it's traded.\n            - `TickSize`: `float64`, minimum price fluctuation.\n            - `LotSize`: `int`, minimum quantity for trading.\n            - `CreatedAt`: `time.Time`, timestamp of creation.\n",
  "instrument-service/internal/handler/instrument_handler.go": "- File Path: `instrument-service/internal/handler/instrument_handler.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements HTTP handlers for instrument-related API endpoints, translating HTTP requests into usecase calls and formatting responses.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Structs:\n        - `InstrumentHandler`: Holds a reference to the `usecase.InstrumentUsecase` to perform business logic.\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewInstrumentHandler(uc usecase.InstrumentUsecase) *InstrumentHandler`: Public function. Constructor for `InstrumentHandler`.\n    - Methods:\n        - `GetAllInstruments(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public method on `InstrumentHandler`. Handles requests to retrieve all instruments. It calls `instrumentUsecase.GetAllInstruments` and responds with a JSON array of instruments or an error.\n",
  "instrument-service/internal/platform/database/postgres.go": "- File Path: `instrument-service/internal/platform/database/postgres.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Manages the PostgreSQL database connection pool and initial schema setup for the `instrument-service`.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewPostgresPool(connStr string) (*pgxpool.Pool, error)`: Public function. Creates and configures a new PostgreSQL connection pool using `pgxpool`. It parses the connection string, sets default pool settings (max connections, lifetime, idle time, health check), and pings the database to verify connectivity.\n        - `InitDatabase(pool *pgxpool.Pool) error`: Public function. Executes SQL to create the `instruments` table if it does not already exist. This function is intended for initial database setup or migrations.\n",
  "instrument-service/internal/repository/instrument_repository.go": "- File Path: `instrument-service/internal/repository/instrument_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the interface for data access operations related to `Instrument` entities, abstracting the underlying data storage mechanism.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Interfaces:\n        - `InstrumentRepository`: Defines the contract for instrument data persistence.\n            - `GetAll(ctx context.Context) ([]*domain.Instrument, error)`: Public method. Retrieves all instruments from the data store.\n            - `Create(ctx context.Context, instrument *domain.Instrument) error`: Public method. Inserts a new instrument into the data store.\n",
  "instrument-service/internal/repository/instrument_repository_postgres.go": "- File Path: `instrument-service/internal/repository/instrument_repository_postgres.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a PostgreSQL-specific implementation of the `InstrumentRepository` interface, handling database interactions for instrument data.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Structs:\n        - `postgresInstrumentRepository`: Implements `InstrumentRepository`, holding a `pgxpool.Pool` instance for database access.\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewPostgresInstrumentRepository(db *pgxpool.Pool) InstrumentRepository`: Public function. Constructor for `postgresInstrumentRepository`.\n    - Methods:\n        - `Create(ctx context.Context, instrument *domain.Instrument) error`: Public method on `postgresInstrumentRepository`. Inserts a new instrument record into the `instruments` table, returning the generated `id` and `created_at` values.\n        - `GetAll(ctx context.Context) ([]*domain.Instrument, error)`: Public method on `postgresInstrumentRepository`. Queries the `instruments` table to retrieve all instrument records, ordered by symbol.\n",
  "instrument-service/internal/usecase/instrument_usecase.go": "- File Path: `instrument-service/internal/usecase/instrument_usecase.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements the business logic for instrument data retrieval.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Interfaces:\n        - `InstrumentUsecase`: Defines the contract for instrument-related business operations.\n            - `GetAllInstruments(ctx context.Context) ([]*domain.Instrument, error)`: Public method. Retrieves all instruments.\n    - Structs:\n        - `instrumentUsecase`: Implements `InstrumentUsecase`, holding a reference to `repository.InstrumentRepository`.\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewInstrumentUsecase(repo repository.InstrumentRepository) InstrumentUsecase`: Public function. Constructor for `instrumentUsecase`.\n    - Methods:\n        - `GetAllInstruments(ctx context.Context) ([]*domain.Instrument, error)`: Public method on `instrumentUsecase`. Delegates the call to the underlying `InstrumentRepository` to fetch all instruments.\n",
  "instrument-service/scripts/seed/Dockerfile": "- File Path: `instrument-service/scripts/seed/Dockerfile`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines a multi-stage Docker build process to create a minimal and efficient Docker image for the Go `instrument-seeder` application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Stages:\n        - `builder`: Uses `golang:1.21-alpine` to download Go modules and build the `seed-instruments` binary from `./scripts/seed` with `CGO_ENABLED=0`.\n        - Final image: Uses `alpine:latest` as a base, adds `ca-certificates`, copies the pre-built binary from the `builder` stage, and defines the command to run the seeder.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Multi-stage build for smaller image size, static compilation of Go application, minimal base image.\n",
  "instrument-service/scripts/seed/main.go": "- File Path: `instrument-service/scripts/seed/main.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Seeds initial instrument data into the PostgreSQL database for the `instrument-service`.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions:\n        - `main()`: Public function.\n            - Loads environment variables from `.env`.\n            - Retrieves `POSTGRES_URL` from environment variables.\n            - Initializes a PostgreSQL connection pool and ensures the `instruments` table exists.\n            - Creates a `repository.NewPostgresInstrumentRepository`.\n            - Defines a slice of `domain.Instrument` with sample data (Equities, Futures, Options).\n            - Iterates through the sample instruments and attempts to create each one in the database, logging success or failure (e.g., due to unique constraint violation).\n",
  "nginx/nginx.conf": "- File Path: `nginx/nginx.conf`\n- High-Level Purpose: Configures Nginx to act as an API Gateway for the GoTrade microservices, routing incoming HTTP and WebSocket requests to the appropriate backend services.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Server Block: Listens on port 80.\n    - Locations:\n        - `/`: Serves a basic \"GoTrade API Gateway\" message (placeholder for frontend).\n        - `/api/user/`: Proxies requests to `user-service:8081`.\n        - `/api/instruments/`: Proxies requests to `instrument-service:8082/instruments/`.\n        - `/api/orders/`: Proxies requests to `order-service:8083/orders/`.\n        - `/api/account/`: Proxies requests to `account-service:8084/account/`.\n        - `/ws`: Proxies WebSocket requests to `websocket-gateway:8085/ws`, handling `Upgrade` and `Connection` headers for WebSocket protocol.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: API Gateway pattern, Reverse Proxy, WebSocket proxying.\n",
  "order-service/Dockerfile": "- File Path: `order-service/Dockerfile`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines a multi-stage Docker build process to create a minimal and efficient Docker image for the Go `order-service` application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Stages:\n        - `builder`: Uses `golang:1.21-alpine` to download Go modules and build the `order-service` binary with `CGO_ENABLED=0` for a static executable.\n        - Final image: Uses `alpine:latest` as a base, adds `ca-certificates`, copies the pre-built binary from the `builder` stage, exposes port 8083, and defines the command to run the service.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Multi-stage build for smaller image size, static compilation of Go application, minimal base image for production.\n",
  "order-service/cmd/server/main.go": "- File Path: `order-service/cmd/server/main.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: The main entry point for the `order-service` application, responsible for configuration loading, database and messaging initialization, dependency injection, HTTP routing, and server lifecycle management, including an outbox poller.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions:\n        - `main()`: Public function.\n            - Loads environment variables from `.env`.\n            - Retrieves `APP_PORT`, `POSTGRES_URL`, `REDIS_URL`, and `JWT_SECRET` from environment variables.\n            - Initializes a PostgreSQL connection pool and runs database migrations (`orders` and `outbox_events` table creation).\n            - Initializes a Redis publisher.\n            - Sets up the application layers: `repository.NewPostgresOrderRepository`, `usecase.NewOrderUsecase`, `handler.NewOrderHandler`.\n            - Starts the `orderUsecase.StartOutboxPolling` in a separate goroutine.\n            - Configures an HTTP router using `go-chi/chi`, including `middleware.Logger` and `middleware.Recoverer`.\n            - Defines public routes (`/health`, `/metrics`).\n            - Defines protected routes (`/orders`, `/orders/{orderID}`) using `handler.JWTAuthMiddleware`.\n            - Starts the HTTP server and implements graceful shutdown on `SIGINT` or `SIGTERM`, also stopping the outbox poller.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Dependency Injection, Layered Architecture (handler -\u003e usecase -\u003e repository -\u003e database/messaging), Graceful Shutdown, Environment Variable Configuration, HTTP Routing with Chi, Transactional Outbox Pattern (with background poller).\n",
  "order-service/go.mod": "- File Path: `order-service/go.mod`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the Go module for the `order-service` and lists its direct dependencies.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Module: `gotrade/order-service`\n    - Go Version: `1.21`\n    - Required Dependencies:\n        - `github.com/go-chi/chi/v5 v5.0.12`: For HTTP routing.\n        - `github.com/golang-jwt/jwt/v5 v5.2.1`: For JWT token handling.\n        - `github.com/google/uuid v1.6.0`: For generating UUIDs.\n        - `github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 v5.5.5`: PostgreSQL driver.\n        - `github.com/joho/godotenv v1.5.1`: For loading environment variables from `.env` files.\n        - `github.com/redis/go-redis/v9 v9.5.1`: Redis client.\n",
  "order-service/internal/domain/order.go": "- File Path: `order-service/internal/domain/order.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the core `Order` entity and `OutboxEvent` structure used within the `order-service` domain.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Types:\n        - `OrderType`: String type for order types (e.g., MARKET, LIMIT).\n        - `OrderSide`: String type for order sides (e.g., BUY, SELL).\n        - `OrderStatus`: String type for order statuses (e.g., OPEN, COMPLETED, CANCELLED, REJECTED).\n    - Constants:\n        - `Market`, `Limit`: `OrderType` constants.\n        - `Buy`, `Sell`: `OrderSide` constants.\n        - `Open`, `Completed`, `Cancelled`, `Rejected`: `OrderStatus` constants.\n    - Structs:\n        - `Order`: Represents a trading order.\n            - `ID`: `int64`, unique identifier.\n            - `UserID`: `int64`, ID of the user placing the order.\n            - `InstrumentID`: `int64`, ID of the instrument being traded.\n            - `Type`: `OrderType`, type of order.\n            - `Side`: `OrderSide`, buy or sell.\n            - `Price`: `float64`, order price (0 for market orders).\n            - `Quantity`: `int`, number of units.\n            - `Status`: `OrderStatus`, current status of the order.\n            - `CreatedAt`: `time.Time`, timestamp of creation.\n            - `UpdatedAt`: `time.Time`, timestamp of last update.\n        - `OutboxEvent`: Represents an event to be published using the transactional outbox pattern.\n            - `ID`: `uuid.UUID`, unique event identifier.\n            - `AggregateID`: `string`, ID of the aggregate (e.g., Order ID).\n            - `AggregateType`: `string`, type of the aggregate (e.g., \"Order\").\n            - `EventType`: `string`, type of the event (e.g., \"OrderPlaced\").\n            - `Payload`: `[]byte`, JSON-marshaled event data.\n            - `CreatedAt`: `time.Time`, timestamp of event creation.\n",
  "order-service/internal/handler/auth_middleware.go": "- File Path: `order-service/internal/handler/auth_middleware.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements an HTTP middleware for authenticating requests using JWT tokens for the `order-service`.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions:\n        - `JWTAuthMiddleware(secret string) func(http.Handler) http.Handler`: Public function. A higher-order function that returns an `http.Handler` middleware. This middleware extracts a JWT from the \"Authorization\" header (Bearer token), validates it using `utils.ValidateJWT`, and if valid, extracts the `userID` from the token claims and adds it to the request context before passing the request to the next handler. It returns `401 Unauthorized` for missing, malformed, or invalid tokens.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Standard Go HTTP middleware pattern, specifically a JWT authentication middleware.\n",
  "order-service/internal/handler/order_handler.go": "- File Path: `order-service/internal/handler/order_handler.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements HTTP handlers for order-related API endpoints, translating HTTP requests into usecase calls and formatting responses.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Structs:\n        - `OrderHandler`: Holds a reference to the `usecase.OrderUsecase` to perform business logic.\n        - `PlaceOrderRequest`: Represents the expected JSON payload for placing an order, with `InstrumentID`, `Type`, `Side`, `Price`, and `Quantity` fields.\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewOrderHandler(uc usecase.OrderUsecase) *OrderHandler`: Public function. Constructor for `OrderHandler`.\n    - Methods:\n        - `PlaceOrder(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public method on `OrderHandler`. Handles requests to place a new order. It extracts `userID` from the request context, decodes the request body, performs basic validation, calls `orderUsecase.PlaceOrder`, and responds with the created order or appropriate error status.\n        - `CancelOrder(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public method on `OrderHandler`. Handles requests to cancel an order. It extracts `userID` from the request context, parses `orderID` from the URL, calls `orderUsecase.CancelOrder`, and responds with the updated order or `404 Not Found` if the order cannot be cancelled.\n",
  "order-service/internal/platform/database/postgres.go": "- File Path: `order-service/internal/platform/database/postgres.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Manages the PostgreSQL database connection pool and initial schema setup for the `order-service`, including `orders` and `outbox_events` tables.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewPostgresPool(connStr string) (*pgxpool.Pool, error)`: Public function. Creates and configures a new PostgreSQL connection pool using `pgxpool`. It parses the connection string, sets default pool settings (max connections, lifetime, idle time, health check), and pings the database to verify connectivity.\n        - `InitDatabase(pool *pgxpool.Pool) error`: Public function. Executes SQL to create the `orders` table and the `outbox_events` table if they do not already exist. This function is intended for initial database setup or migrations.\n",
  "order-service/internal/platform/messaging/redis.go": "- File Path: `order-service/internal/platform/messaging/redis.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a Redis client for publishing messages, specifically designed for the `order-service`'s messaging needs.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Structs:\n        - `RedisPublisher`: Holds a `*redis.Client` instance for Redis interactions.\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewRedisPublisher(redisAddr string) (*RedisPublisher, error)`: Public function. Constructor for `RedisPublisher`. Initializes a new Redis client and pings it to verify connectivity.\n    - Methods:\n        - `Publish(ctx context.Context, channel string, message []byte) error`: Public method on `RedisPublisher`. Publishes a `message` (byte slice) to a specified Redis `channel`.\n        - `Close() error`: Public method on `RedisPublisher`. Closes the underlying Redis client connection.\n",
  "order-service/internal/repository/order_repository.go": "- File Path: `order-service/internal/repository/order_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the interface for data access operations related to `Order` and `OutboxEvent` entities, abstracting the underlying data storage mechanism.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Interfaces:\n        - `OrderRepository`: Defines the contract for order and outbox event persistence.\n            - `CreateOrderWithOutbox(ctx context.Context, order *domain.Order, event *domain.OutboxEvent) error`: Public method. Creates a new order and an associated outbox event within a single transaction.\n            - `UpdateOrderStatus(ctx context.Context, orderID int64, userID int64, status domain.OrderStatus) (*domain.Order, error)`: Public method. Updates the status of an existing order for a specific user.\n            - `GetOpenOrdersByUserID(ctx context.Context, userID int64) ([]*domain.Order, error)`: Public method. Retrieves all open orders for a given user.\n            - `GetOrderHistoryByUserID(ctx context.Context, userID int64) ([]*domain.Order, error)`: Public method. Retrieves the history of non-open orders for a given user.\n            - `GetPollingOutboxEvents(ctx context.Context, limit int) ([]domain.OutboxEvent, error)`: Public method. Retrieves a limited number of outbox events for processing, using `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` for concurrency.\n            - `DeleteOutboxEvents(ctx context.Context, tx pgx.Tx, eventIDs []string) error`: Public method. Deletes a list of processed outbox events within a provided transaction.\n",
  "order-service/internal/repository/order_repository_postgres.go": "- File Path: `order-service/internal/repository/order_repository_postgres.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a PostgreSQL-specific implementation of the `OrderRepository` interface, handling database interactions for order and outbox event data, including transactional operations.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Structs:\n        - `postgresOrderRepository`: Implements `OrderRepository`, holding a `pgxpool.Pool` instance for database access.\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewPostgresOrderRepository(db *pgxpool.Pool) OrderRepository`: Public function. Constructor for `postgresOrderRepository`.\n    - Methods:\n        - `CreateOrderWithOutbox(ctx context.Context, order *domain.Order, event *domain.OutboxEvent) error`: Public method on `postgresOrderRepository`. Inserts a new order and a corresponding outbox event into their respective tables within a single PostgreSQL transaction.\n        - `UpdateOrderStatus(ctx context.Context, orderID int64, userID int64, status domain.OrderStatus) (*domain.Order, error)`: Public method on `postgresOrderRepository`. Updates the status of an order for a specific user, ensuring the order is currently 'OPEN'. Returns the updated order or `nil` if not found/updatable.\n        - `GetOpenOrdersByUserID(ctx context.Context, userID int64) ([]*domain.Order, error)`: Public method on `postgresOrderRepository`. Retrieves all orders with `status = 'OPEN'` for a given user.\n        - `GetOrderHistoryByUserID(ctx context.Context, userID int64) ([]*domain.Order, error)`: Public method on `postgresOrderRepository`. Retrieves all orders with `status != 'OPEN'` (i.e., completed, cancelled, rejected) for a given user.\n        - `queryOrders(ctx context.Context, query string, args ...interface{}) ([]*domain.Order, error)`: Internal method on `postgresOrderRepository`. A helper function to execute a given SQL query and scan the results into a slice of `domain.Order` pointers.\n        - `GetPollingOutboxEvents(ctx context.Context, limit int) ([]domain.OutboxEvent, error)`: Public method on `postgresOrderRepository`. Selects a limited number of outbox events, ordered by creation time, using `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` to prevent concurrent processing.\n        - `DeleteOutboxEvents(ctx context.Context, tx pgx.Tx, eventIDs []string) error`: Public method on `postgresOrderRepository`. Deletes a list of outbox events by their IDs within a provided PostgreSQL transaction.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Transactional Outbox Pattern (ensuring atomicity of order creation and event persistence), `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` for concurrent outbox polling.",
  "order-service/internal/usecase/order_usecase.go": "- File Path: `order-service/internal/usecase/order_usecase.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements the business logic for order management, including placing and canceling orders, and managing the transactional outbox pattern for event publishing.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Interfaces:\n        - `OrderUsecase`: Defines the contract for order-related business operations.\n            - `PlaceOrder(ctx context.Context, userID int64, instrumentID int64, orderType domain.OrderType, side domain.OrderSide, price float64, quantity int) (*domain.Order, error)`: Public method. Handles placing a new order.\n            - `CancelOrder(ctx context.Context, userID int64, orderID int64) (*domain.Order, error)`: Public method. Handles canceling an existing order.\n            - `StartOutboxPolling(ctx context.Context)`: Public method. Initiates a background process to poll and publish outbox events.\n        - `MessagePublisher`: Defines the contract for publishing messages.\n            - `Publish(ctx context.Context, channel string, message []byte) error`: Public method. Publishes a message to a specified channel.\n    - Structs:\n        - `orderUsecase`: Implements `OrderUsecase`, holding references to `repository.OrderRepository`, `MessagePublisher`, and `pgxpool.Pool`.\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewOrderUsecase(repo repository.OrderRepository, publisher MessagePublisher, dbPool *pgxpool.Pool) OrderUsecase`: Public function. Constructor for `orderUsecase`.\n    - Methods:\n        - `PlaceOrder(ctx context.Context, userID int64, instrumentID int64, orderType domain.OrderType, side domain.OrderSide, price float64, quantity int) (*domain.Order, error)`: Public method on `orderUsecase`. Creates an `Order` and an `OutboxEvent`, then calls the repository to persist both transactionally. It also immediately publishes the event to Redis (with a note about potential race conditions).\n        - `CancelOrder(ctx context.Context, userID int64, orderID int64) (*domain.Order, error)`: Public method on `orderUsecase`. Updates an order's status to `Cancelled` via the repository and publishes a corresponding event to Redis.\n        - `StartOutboxPolling(ctx context.Context)`: Public method on `orderUsecase`. Runs a ticker-based loop to continuously call `pollAndPublish` until the provided context is cancelled.\n        - `pollAndPublish(ctx context.Context)`: Internal method on `orderUsecase`. Retrieves a batch of outbox events from the repository within a transaction, attempts to publish them to Redis, and then deletes successfully published events from the outbox table.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Transactional Outbox Pattern, Event-Driven Architecture (publishing to Redis), Background Polling, Dependency Injection.\n",
  "order-service/pkg/utils/jwt.go": "- File Path: `order-service/pkg/utils/jwt.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides utility functions for generating and validating JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) within the `order-service`.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Structs:\n        - `JWTClaims`: Custom JWT claims structure, embedding `jwt.RegisteredClaims` and adding a `UserID` field.\n            - `UserID`: `int64`, the ID of the user.\n            - `RegisteredClaims`: Standard JWT claims (e.g., `ExpiresAt`, `IssuedAt`).\n    - Functions:\n        - `GenerateJWT(userID int64, secret string) (string, error)`: Public function. Creates a new JWT token for a given `userID`, signing it with the provided `secret`. The token includes `user_id`, `expiration` (72 hours), and `issued at` claims.\n        - `ValidateJWT(tokenString string, secret string) (*jwt.Token, error)`: Public function. Parses and validates a JWT `tokenString` using the provided `secret` and `JWTClaims` structure. It ensures the signing method is HMAC.\n",
  "user-service/Dockerfile": "- File Path: `user-service/Dockerfile`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines a multi-stage Docker build process to create a minimal and efficient Docker image for the Go `user-service` application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Stages:\n        - `builder`: Uses `golang:1.21-alpine` to download Go modules and build the `user-service` binary with `CGO_ENABLED=0` for a static executable.\n        - Final image: Uses `alpine:latest` as a base, adds `ca-certificates`, copies the pre-built binary from the `builder` stage, exposes port 8081, and defines the command to run the service.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Multi-stage build for smaller image size, static compilation of Go application, minimal base image for production.\n",
  "user-service/go.mod": "- File Path: `user-service/go.mod`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the Go module for the `user-service` and lists its direct dependencies.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Module: `gotrade/user-service`\n    - Go Version: `1.21`\n    - Required Dependencies:\n        - `github.com/go-chi/chi/v5 v5.0.12`: For HTTP routing.\n        - `github.com/golang-jwt/jwt/v5 v5.2.1`: For JWT token handling.\n        - `github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 v5.5.5`: PostgreSQL driver.\n        - `github.com/joho/godotenv v1.5.1`: For loading environment variables from `.env` files.\n        - `golang.org/x/crypto v0.22.0`: For cryptographic functions, specifically bcrypt.\n",
  "user-service/go.sum": "- File Path: `user-service/go.sum`\n- High-Level Purpose: Contains cryptographic checksums for the direct and indirect dependencies of the `user-service` Go module, ensuring build integrity and reproducibility.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Lists module paths and their corresponding cryptographic hashes for both the module itself and its `go.mod` file. This file is automatically generated and managed by Go modules.\n",
  "user-service/internal/domain/user.go": "- File Path: `user-service/internal/domain/user.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the core `User` entity structure used throughout the `user-service` domain.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Structs:\n        - `User`: Represents a user in the system.\n            - `ID`: `int64`, primary identifier, JSON field `id`.\n            - `Email`: `string`, user's email address, JSON field `email`.\n            - `Password`: `string`, user's hashed password, omitted from JSON responses (`json:\"-\"`).\n            - `CreatedAt`: `time.Time`, timestamp of user creation, JSON field `created_at`.\n",
  "user-service/internal/handler/auth_middleware.go": "- File Path: `user-service/internal/handler/auth_middleware.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements an HTTP middleware for authenticating requests using JWT tokens.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions:\n        - `JWTAuthMiddleware(secret string) func(http.Handler) http.Handler`: Public function. A higher-order function that returns an `http.Handler` middleware. This middleware extracts a JWT from the \"Authorization\" header (Bearer token), validates it using `utils.ValidateJWT`, and if valid, extracts the `userID` from the token claims and adds it to the request context before passing the request to the next handler.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Standard Go HTTP middleware pattern, specifically a JWT authentication middleware.\n",
  "user-service/internal/handler/user_handler.go": "- File Path: `user-service/internal/handler/user_handler.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements HTTP handlers for user-related API endpoints, translating HTTP requests into usecase calls and formatting responses.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Structs:\n        - `UserHandler`: Holds a reference to the `usecase.UserUsecase` to perform business logic.\n        - `RegisterRequest`: Represents the expected JSON payload for user registration, with `Email` and `Password` fields.\n        - `LoginRequest`: Represents the expected JSON payload for user login, with `Email` and `Password` fields.\n        - `LoginResponse`: Represents the JSON response for successful login, containing a `Token`.\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewUserHandler(uc usecase.UserUsecase) *UserHandler`: Public function. Constructor for `UserHandler`.\n    - Methods:\n        - `Register(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public method on `UserHandler`. Handles user registration requests. Decodes the request body, calls `userUsecase.Register`, and responds with the created user or appropriate error status (e.g., `409 Conflict` for existing user).\n        - `Login(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public method on `UserHandler`. Handles user login requests. Decodes the request body, calls `userUsecase.Login`, and responds with a JWT token or `401 Unauthorized` for invalid credentials.\n        - `GetProfile(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Public method on `UserHandler`. Handles requests to retrieve the authenticated user's profile. Extracts `userID` from the request context (set by middleware), calls `userUsecase.GetUserProfile`, and responds with the user data or `404 Not Found`.\n",
  "user-service/internal/platform/database/postgres.go": "- File Path: `user-service/internal/platform/database/postgres.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Manages the PostgreSQL database connection pool and initial schema setup for the `user-service`.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewPostgresPool(connStr string) (*pgxpool.Pool, error)`: Public function. Creates and configures a new PostgreSQL connection pool using `pgxpool`. It parses the connection string, sets default pool settings (max connections, lifetime, idle time, health check), and pings the database to verify connectivity.\n        - `InitDatabase(pool *pgxpool.Pool) error`: Public function. Executes SQL to create the `users` table if it does not already exist. This function is intended for initial database setup or migrations.\n",
  "user-service/internal/repository/user_repository.go": "- File Path: `user-service/internal/repository/user_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the interface for data access operations related to `User` entities, abstracting the underlying data storage mechanism.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Interfaces:\n        - `UserRepository`: Defines the contract for user data persistence.\n            - `Create(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error`: Public method. Inserts a new user into the data store.\n            - `FindByEmail(ctx context.Context, email string) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method. Retrieves a user by their email address.\n            - `FindByID(ctx context.Context, id int64) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method. Retrieves a user by their unique ID.\n",
  "user-service/internal/repository/user_repository_postgres.go": "- File Path: `user-service/internal/repository/user_repository_postgres.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a PostgreSQL-specific implementation of the `UserRepository` interface, handling database interactions for user data.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Structs:\n        - `postgresUserRepository`: Implements `UserRepository`, holding a `pgxpool.Pool` instance for database access.\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewPostgresUserRepository(db *pgxpool.Pool) UserRepository`: Public function. Constructor for `postgresUserRepository`.\n    - Methods:\n        - `Create(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error`: Public method on `postgresUserRepository`. Inserts a new user record into the `users` table, returning the generated `id` and `created_at` values.\n        - `FindByEmail(ctx context.Context, email string) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method on `postgresUserRepository`. Queries the `users` table to find a user by their email. Returns `nil, nil` if no user is found (handling `pgx.ErrNoRows`).\n        - `FindByID(ctx context.Context, id int64) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method on `postgresUserRepository`. Queries the `users` table to find a user by their ID. Returns `nil, nil` if no user is found.\n",
  "user-service/internal/usecase/user_usecase.go": "- File Path: `user-service/internal/usecase/user_usecase.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements the business logic for user management, orchestrating interactions between handlers, repositories, and utility functions.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Interfaces:\n        - `UserUsecase`: Defines the contract for user-related business operations.\n            - `Register(ctx context.Context, email, password string) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method. Handles user registration.\n            - `Login(ctx context.Context, email, password string) (string, error)`: Public method. Handles user login.\n            - `GetUserProfile(ctx context.Context, userID int64) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method. Retrieves a user's profile.\n    - Structs:\n        - `userUsecase`: Implements `UserUsecase`, holding references to `repository.UserRepository` and the `jwtSecret`.\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewUserUsecase(userRepo repository.UserRepository, jwtSecret string) UserUsecase`: Public function. Constructor for `userUsecase`.\n    - Methods:\n        - `Register(ctx context.Context, email, password string) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method on `userUsecase`. Checks if a user with the email already exists, hashes the password, and creates the user via the repository. Returns `ErrUserAlreadyExists` if the email is taken.\n        - `Login(ctx context.Context, email, password string) (string, error)`: Public method on `userUsecase`. Finds the user by email, checks the password hash, and if valid, generates a JWT token. Returns `ErrInvalidCredentials` for incorrect email or password.\n        - `GetUserProfile(ctx context.Context, userID int64) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method on `userUsecase`. Retrieves a user's profile by ID using the repository. Returns `ErrUserNotFound` if the user does not exist.\n    - Variables:\n        - `ErrUserAlreadyExists`: `error`, module-level, exported.\n        - `ErrInvalidCredentials`: `error`, module-level, exported.\n        - `ErrUserNotFound`: `error`, module-level, exported.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Encapsulates business rules, uses exported errors for specific error conditions, orchestrates calls to repository and utility functions.",
  "user-service/main.go": "- File Path: `user-service/main.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: The main entry point for the `user-service` application, responsible for configuration loading, database initialization, dependency injection, HTTP routing, and server lifecycle management.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions:\n        - `main()`: Public function.\n            - Loads environment variables from `.env`.\n            - Retrieves `APP_PORT`, `POSTGRES_URL`, and `JWT_SECRET` from environment variables.\n            - Initializes a PostgreSQL connection pool and runs database migrations (`users` table creation).\n            - Sets up the application layers: `repository.NewPostgresUserRepository`, `usecase.NewUserUsecase`, `handler.NewUserHandler`.\n            - Configures an HTTP router using `go-chi/chi`, including `middleware.Logger` and `middleware.Recoverer`.\n            - Defines public routes (`/health`, `/metrics`, `/register`, `/login`).\n            - Defines protected routes (`/me`) using `handler.JWTAuthMiddleware`.\n            - Starts the HTTP server and implements graceful shutdown on `SIGINT` or `SIGTERM`.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Dependency Injection, Layered Architecture (handler -\u003e usecase -\u003e repository -\u003e database), Graceful Shutdown, Environment Variable Configuration, HTTP Routing with Chi.\n",
  "user-service/pkg/utils/hash.go": "- File Path: `user-service/pkg/utils/hash.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides utility functions for securely hashing and verifying passwords using the bcrypt algorithm.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions:\n        - `HashPassword(password string) (string, error)`: Public function. Generates a bcrypt hash for the given plain `password` with a cost of 14.\n        - `CheckPasswordHash(password, hash string) bool`: Public function. Compares a plain `password` against a bcrypt `hash` to determine if they match. Returns `true` if they match, `false` otherwise.\n",
  "user-service/pkg/utils/jwt.go": "- File Path: `user-service/pkg/utils/jwt.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides utility functions for generating and validating JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) within the `user-service`.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions:\n        - `GenerateJWT(userID int64, secret string) (string, error)`: Public function. Creates a new JWT token for a given `userID`, signing it with the provided `secret`. The token includes `user_id`, `expiration` (72 hours), and `issued at` claims.\n        - `ValidateJWT(tokenString string, secret string) (*jwt.Token, error)`: Public function. Parses and validates a JWT `tokenString` using the provided `secret`. It ensures the signing method is HMAC.\n",
  "websocket-gateway/Dockerfile": "- File Path: `websocket-gateway/Dockerfile`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines a multi-stage Docker build process to create a minimal and efficient Docker image for the Go `websocket-gateway` application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Stages:\n        - `builder`: Uses `golang:1.21-alpine` to download Go modules and build the `gateway` binary with `CGO_ENABLED=0` for a static executable.\n        - Final image: Uses `alpine:latest` as a base, adds `ca-certificates`, copies the pre-built binary from the `builder` stage, exposes port 8085, and defines the command to run the service.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Multi-stage build for smaller image size, static compilation of Go application, minimal base image for production.\n",
  "websocket-gateway/cmd/server/main.go": "- File Path: `websocket-gateway/cmd/server/main.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: The main entry point for the `websocket-gateway` application, responsible for loading configuration, initializing the WebSocket hub, and serving WebSocket connections.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Variables:\n        - `upgrader`: `websocket.Upgrader`, module-level. Configures WebSocket upgrade parameters, allowing all origins for simplicity.\n    - Functions:\n        - `serveWs(hub *hub.Hub, w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: Internal function. Upgrades an HTTP request to a WebSocket connection and registers the new client with the `hub`.\n        - `main()`: Public function.\n            - Loads environment variables from `.env`.\n            - Retrieves `APP_PORT` and `REDIS_URL` from environment variables, exiting if `REDIS_URL` is not set.\n            - Initializes a `hub.Hub` instance.\n            - Starts the `hub.Run()` method in a separate goroutine.\n            - Registers the `/ws` HTTP endpoint to handle WebSocket upgrade requests using `serveWs`.\n            - Starts the HTTP server to listen for incoming connections.\n",
  "websocket-gateway/go.mod": "- File Path: `websocket-gateway/go.mod`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the Go module for the `websocket-gateway` and lists its direct dependencies.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Module: `gotrade/websocket-gateway`\n    - Go Version: `1.21`\n    - Required Dependencies:\n        - `github.com/gorilla/websocket v1.5.1`: For WebSocket communication.\n        - `github.com/joho/godotenv v1.5.1`: For loading environment variables from `.env` files.\n        - `github.com/redis/go-redis/v9 v9.5.1`: Redis client.\n    - Indirect Dependencies: Includes `github.com/cespare/xxhash/v2`, `github.com/dgryski/go-rendezvous`, `golang.org/x/net`.\n",
  "websocket-gateway/internal/client/client.go": "- File Path: `websocket-gateway/internal/client/client.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Manages individual WebSocket client connections, handling message reading, writing, and ping/pong heartbeats to maintain connection liveness.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Constants:\n        - `writeWait`: `10 * time.Second`, time allowed to write a message to the peer.\n        - `pongWait`: `60 * time.Second`, time allowed to read the next pong message from the peer.\n        - `pingPeriod`: `(pongWait * 9) / 10`, send pings to peer with this period. Must be less than `pongWait`.\n        - `maxMessageSize`: `512`, maximum message size allowed from peer.\n    - Structs:\n        - `Client`: Represents a single WebSocket client connection.\n            - `Conn`: `*websocket.Conn`, the underlying WebSocket connection.\n            - `Send`: `chan []byte`, a buffered channel for outbound messages to the client.\n    - Methods:\n        - `ReadPump(unregister func(*Client))`: Public method on `Client`. Pumps messages from the WebSocket connection. It sets read limits and pong handlers, and calls the `unregister` function if the connection closes unexpectedly or an error occurs.\n        - `WritePump()`: Public method on `Client`. Pumps messages from the `Send` channel to the WebSocket connection. It handles writing messages, sending periodic ping messages, and closing the connection if the `Send` channel is closed or a write error occurs.",
  "websocket-gateway/internal/hub/hub.go": "- File Path: `websocket-gateway/internal/hub/hub.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Manages WebSocket clients, broadcasts messages to them, and subscribes to Redis Pub/Sub channels to receive and forward real-time events.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Structs:\n        - `Hub`: Manages the lifecycle of WebSocket clients.\n            - `clients`: `map[*client.Client]bool`, stores active clients.\n            - `broadcast`: `chan []byte`, channel for messages to be broadcast to all clients.\n            - `register`: `chan *client.Client`, channel for new client registrations.\n            - `unregister`: `chan *client.Client`, channel for client unregistrations.\n            - `redisClient`: `*redis.Client`, Redis client for Pub/Sub.\n    - Functions:\n        - `NewHub(redisAddr string) (*Hub, error)`: Public function. Constructor for `Hub`. Initializes a Redis client and pings it to verify connectivity.\n    - Methods:\n        - `Run()`: Public method on `Hub`. Starts the main event loop for the hub, handling client registration/unregistration and message broadcasting. Also starts the `subscribeToRedis` goroutine.\n        - `RegisterClient(conn *websocket.Conn)`: Public method on `Hub`. Creates a new `client.Client` from a WebSocket connection, registers it with the hub, and starts its `WritePump` and `ReadPump` goroutines.\n        - `subscribeToRedis()`: Internal method on `Hub`. Subscribes to the \"orders\" Redis channel and forwards any received messages to the `broadcast` channel.\n"
